<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi's Arab National Bank nine-month net rises.</title>
<headline>Saudi's Arab National Bank nine-month net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>		    (billion riyals unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit			   350.4 million    vs  299.2 million</p>
<p>Operating income		     1.62	 vs    1.67</p>
<p> Operating expenses		   1.30	 vs    1.38</p>
<p> Loan loss provision		 54.9 million    vs   37.7 million</p>
<p> Total deposits			22.34	 vs   20.77</p>
<p> Net loans and advances	     9.36	 vs   10.58</p>
<p> Net investment portfolio	  10.14	 vs    9.09</p>
<p>Shareholders' equity		 2.97	 vs    2.81</p>
<p> Assets				  32.96	 vs   31.66</p>
<p>Full name: Arab National Bank.</p>
<p>NOTE: Based in Saudi Arabia, Arab National Bank is 40 percent owned by the Amman-based Arab Bank Ltd. The rest is held by Saudi investors.</p>
</text>
